1
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:06,940
C'mon, now, don't ignore me!

2
00:00:08,990 --> 00:00:09,880
Hey!

3
00:00:09,880 --> 00:00:11,610
Ow!

4
00:00:11,610 --> 00:00:14,000
Ow! That hurts!

5
00:00:11,610 --> 00:00:16,180
What's the problem? You train every day, 
and you still lose to one middle-aged man?

6
00:00:16,180 --> 00:00:17,530
Ow, ow, ow, ow!

7
00:00:16,180 --> 00:00:17,530
Whoa, wait a—

8
00:00:17,530 --> 00:00:20,160
Ow, ow, ow, ow, ow!

9
00:00:18,550 --> 00:00:21,380
Letting me get a counter in? 
You're getting old, Pops!

10
00:00:21,380 --> 00:00:22,660
I'm about to win by decisio—

11
00:00:22,660 --> 00:00:26,360
Hey, wait! No fair flipping me back over!

12
00:00:24,980 --> 00:00:27,630
Well? Ready to give up?

13
00:00:26,830 --> 00:00:27,630
Ow, ow!

14
00:00:28,180 --> 00:00:31,310
Excuse me, you two...

15
00:00:32,330 --> 00:00:37,260
I'm getting hungry. I'd like
 to eat breakfast now.

16
00:00:37,260 --> 00:00:38,810
Whoops...

17
00:00:38,810 --> 00:00:40,010
Sorry about that.

18
00:00:40,010 --> 00:00:42,920
I got a little carried away with 
my one-on-one time with Subaru.

19
00:00:42,920 --> 00:00:44,990
You could've started without us.

20
00:00:44,990 --> 00:00:48,360
Why should I do that when the 
whole family could eat together?

21
00:00:48,360 --> 00:00:51,320
Yeah, you're right. That's my wife for ya!

22
00:00:51,720 --> 00:00:54,170
Come on, Subaru. Time for breakfast.

23
00:00:54,930 --> 00:00:59,030
I put in extra effort today, just for you.

24
00:01:01,970 --> 00:01:05,890
Wow, Subaru. Your bowl's a forest of green.

25
00:01:05,890 --> 00:01:09,710
Mom, why did you give me so many peas?

26
00:01:09,710 --> 00:01:12,200
It's not good to be picky about your food.

27
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:15,330
I thought this might be a good 
chance to get you over that.

28
00:01:15,330 --> 00:01:19,460
What "chance"? This isn't a 
special day or anything.

29
00:01:17,860 --> 00:01:20,610
Very naïve of you, Subaru. Today is...

30
00:01:20,610 --> 00:01:26,190
No, every moment of every day is 
a precious, once-in-a-lifetime moment.

31
00:01:25,480 --> 00:01:27,520
That's irrelevant right now.

32
00:01:27,770 --> 00:01:28,920
I'm digging in.

33
00:01:28,920 --> 00:01:30,770
Yes, go right ahead.

34
00:01:31,520 --> 00:01:35,150
I've always wondered... Why the 
mix of Japanese and Western dishes?

35
00:01:35,150 --> 00:01:37,970
My favorite thing to put in 
miso soup is wakame seaweed,

36
00:01:37,970 --> 00:01:40,320
and I like strawberry jam on my toast.

37
00:01:42,880 --> 00:01:46,250
What are we gonna do with this? 
We just keep passing it around...

38
00:01:46,250 --> 00:01:48,950
Well, I hate peas, you know.

39
00:01:48,950 --> 00:01:51,530
And you were trying to make 
<i>me</i> stop being picky?!

40
00:01:51,530 --> 00:01:53,180
Don't get the wrong idea, though.

41
00:01:53,180 --> 00:01:57,260
I hate all foods that are tiny and round.

42
00:01:56,530 --> 00:01:58,260
I didn't have any wrong ideas!

43
00:01:58,260 --> 00:02:00,870
If anything, I have even more doubts now!

44
00:02:00,870 --> 00:02:03,580
Okay, then. The husband should 
take responsibility for his wife.

45
00:02:04,400 --> 00:02:08,700
Subaru, families that get along as 
well as ours are rare these days.

46
00:02:09,140 --> 00:02:12,820
In other words, I hate the same 
things you and your mother hate!

47
00:02:13,170 --> 00:02:16,690
This forest of green was never 
going to make anyone happy, then!

48
00:02:16,690 --> 00:02:19,110
I'll just make it into something 
we all love: pilaf!

49
00:02:20,800 --> 00:02:23,120
I can't even stand to look at it.

50
00:02:27,870 --> 00:02:28,830
Subaru.

51
00:02:28,830 --> 00:02:29,710
Right.

52
00:02:31,260 --> 00:02:33,140
Thank you for breakfast.

53
00:02:33,140 --> 00:02:34,290
My pleasure!

54
00:02:34,290 --> 00:02:35,960
Now, let's get the dishes to the sink,

55
00:02:35,960 --> 00:02:38,400
and we'll race to school to help us digest!

56
00:02:38,400 --> 00:02:42,440
Quit making this a scenario that 
ends with me going to school.

57
00:02:43,300 --> 00:02:44,560
I'm sleeping in until noon.

58
00:02:45,440 --> 00:02:46,640
Ow...

59
00:02:47,240 --> 00:02:48,500
Subaru?

60
00:02:48,500 --> 00:02:49,940
It's nothing.

61
00:02:56,360 --> 00:02:57,700
What the hell? Why?

62
00:02:58,150 --> 00:03:00,530
Why do I suddenly feel so weird?

63
00:03:10,060 --> 00:03:11,920
Once it's past eight...

64
00:03:29,320 --> 00:03:31,740
I won't make it to school on time now.

65
00:03:32,570 --> 00:03:35,560
So there's no other choice. 
I have no choice...

66
00:03:37,440 --> 00:03:38,480
Why?

67
00:03:38,480 --> 00:03:40,780
That normally calms it down...

68
00:03:45,560 --> 00:03:48,250
Mind if I come in, Subaru?

69
00:03:48,920 --> 00:03:53,400
What's the point of asking if you 
come in before I can answer?

70
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:57,320
There's no need for that between 
two guys as tight as you and—

71
00:03:57,320 --> 00:03:58,700
Wait, I guess there is!

72
00:03:58,700 --> 00:04:01,590
Sorry, I forgot you're a teenager! 
I'll leave and come back!

73
00:04:01,590 --> 00:04:03,600
I wasn't doing anything!

74
00:04:03,970 --> 00:04:04,680
So?

75
00:04:06,210 --> 00:04:07,560
Well...

76
00:04:08,680 --> 00:04:11,100
Subaru, is there a girl you like?

77
00:04:11,400 --> 00:04:12,900
Are we in middle school now?!

78
00:04:13,440 --> 00:04:14,560
You're no fun.

79
00:04:14,560 --> 00:04:17,420
So, what do you actually want?

80
00:04:17,420 --> 00:04:19,980
Oh, well, you know...

81
00:04:19,980 --> 00:04:21,570
The weather's nice, so...

82
00:04:22,700 --> 00:04:26,160
Let's go have a nice father-son talk outside.

83
00:04:33,670 --> 00:04:36,500
Man, what's with everyone?

84
00:04:36,500 --> 00:04:40,340
They happen to see me on my day off, 
and they all assume I lost my job.

85
00:04:42,280 --> 00:04:46,480
Hey, don't make such a gloomy face 
on a nice morning like this.

86
00:04:46,480 --> 00:04:49,340
It's your own fault for dragging me out here.

87
00:04:49,340 --> 00:04:51,560
Don't act all suspicious.

88
00:04:51,560 --> 00:04:53,920
I'm not gonna tell you anything scary.

89
00:04:53,920 --> 00:04:55,950
It's more of a father-son subject.

90
00:04:55,950 --> 00:04:58,050
A father-son subject, huh?

91
00:04:58,480 --> 00:05:01,460
Ken, my boy! Haven't seen you in a while.

92
00:05:01,460 --> 00:05:03,930
Oh? Don't tell me that's...

93
00:05:04,480 --> 00:05:06,980
Yep, that's right. He's my son...

94
00:05:06,980 --> 00:05:10,820
Actually, I should say he's my pride and joy.

95
00:05:10,820 --> 00:05:13,670
Ah, so I was right.

96
00:05:13,670 --> 00:05:16,730
He looks so much like you 
did when you were...

97
00:05:16,730 --> 00:05:19,710
Actually, no, you don't. 
Do you take after your mom?

98
00:05:20,080 --> 00:05:23,660
Uh... Well, a lot of people say I do.

99
00:05:23,660 --> 00:05:25,290
My eyes, especially.

100
00:05:25,290 --> 00:05:26,830
I see.

101
00:05:26,830 --> 00:05:31,080
Hard to believe you're old enough 
to have a son that age.

102
00:05:32,080 --> 00:05:33,020
Come to think of it...

103
00:05:33,360 --> 00:05:35,470
Today's Monday, isn't it?

104
00:05:35,470 --> 00:05:37,850
What are you doing out here 
with your dad at this hour?

105
00:05:42,650 --> 00:05:44,080
Sorry...

106
00:05:45,130 --> 00:05:46,280
Hey, Subaru!

107
00:05:48,360 --> 00:05:52,380
Sorry about that. We'll stop by 
again when we have time to chat.

108
00:05:52,380 --> 00:05:56,290
Ah, sure. Looks like I said 
something I shouldn't have.

109
00:05:56,540 --> 00:05:58,420
Apologize to him for me, would you?

110
00:05:58,680 --> 00:06:01,170
You have nothing to apologize for.

111
00:06:01,580 --> 00:06:04,380
It's up to him to deal with it himself now.

112
00:06:06,010 --> 00:06:09,720
Here ya go. A tasty, ice-cold 
cola packed with my love.

113
00:06:15,030 --> 00:06:18,440
Don't cluck your tongue at me.
I know how you think.

114
00:06:18,440 --> 00:06:20,250
Ugh, my hand's all sticky now.

115
00:06:22,500 --> 00:06:24,610
Well? Feel better now?

116
00:06:25,120 --> 00:06:26,350
Hard to say.

117
00:06:27,040 --> 00:06:29,750
You look like you're really not feeling well.

118
00:06:30,160 --> 00:06:33,250
Want to go home? I can carry you on my back.

119
00:06:33,250 --> 00:06:36,410
You don't have to do that, 
and I don't need to go home.

120
00:06:37,360 --> 00:06:39,870
It'd be the same at home, anyway.

121
00:06:46,300 --> 00:06:49,590
Listen, Subaru... Not to 
change the subject, but...

122
00:06:51,290 --> 00:06:53,550
Is there a girl you like?

123
00:06:57,760 --> 00:06:58,270
<i>Subaru...</i>

124
00:06:59,160 --> 00:06:59,760
Huh?

125
00:07:03,790 --> 00:07:04,560
What's up?

126
00:07:05,020 --> 00:07:07,950
Wait... did someone just say my name?

127
00:07:08,810 --> 00:07:09,820
No...

128
00:07:12,690 --> 00:07:14,780
What the heck was that, then?

129
00:07:16,800 --> 00:07:19,360
So? Is there a girl you like?

130
00:07:19,360 --> 00:07:21,140
Why do you keep asking that?

131
00:07:21,140 --> 00:07:23,100
You can stop beating around the bush.

132
00:07:23,660 --> 00:07:27,630
Just come out and ask me 
why I didn't go to school.

133
00:07:28,360 --> 00:07:32,120
And here I was trying to 
be considerate for once.

134
00:07:32,650 --> 00:07:37,820
Well, that <i>is</i> what I wanted to 
talk about, so you're not wrong.

135
00:07:40,080 --> 00:07:43,250
I know it's disrespectful to you and Mom.

136
00:07:43,250 --> 00:07:45,860
There's no need to feel that way.

137
00:07:45,860 --> 00:07:48,780
I do have the vague sense that 
you have your reasons for it,

138
00:07:49,050 --> 00:07:50,360
and even if you don't,

139
00:07:50,360 --> 00:07:53,800
I'm prepared to brush it off as 
something I can't do anything about.

140
00:07:59,360 --> 00:08:02,360
I don't know about the rest of the world,

141
00:08:02,360 --> 00:08:05,430
but I personally don't believe 
school is everything.

142
00:08:05,430 --> 00:08:06,810
I mean, what's the big deal?

143
00:08:08,880 --> 00:08:09,510
Why?

144
00:08:12,590 --> 00:08:16,140
Why did you suddenly decide 
to tell me all this today?

145
00:08:16,770 --> 00:08:20,640
It's not like today is a 
special day or anything.

146
00:08:20,640 --> 00:08:23,460
It's just... Peas Day.

147
00:08:25,090 --> 00:08:28,040
Well, your bowl was certainly full of them.

148
00:08:30,120 --> 00:08:32,090
I'm not sure why.

149
00:08:32,710 --> 00:08:36,700
I guess the look on your face this 
morning seemed a little better.

150
00:08:37,390 --> 00:08:39,730
My face... looked better?

151
00:08:39,730 --> 00:08:41,730
The <i>look</i> on your face.

152
00:08:41,730 --> 00:08:43,440
Your face still looks like a bad guy's,

153
00:08:43,440 --> 00:08:46,710
with those mean eyes you got from your mom.

154
00:08:47,820 --> 00:08:50,690
Nothing about me has changed!

155
00:08:50,690 --> 00:08:53,720
That's how I want it, and that's how I'll—

156
00:08:55,900 --> 00:08:58,530
Hey, you look like you're really in pain!

157
00:08:58,530 --> 00:08:59,850
Are you okay?

158
00:09:02,120 --> 00:09:03,340
Subaru...

159
00:09:07,230 --> 00:09:09,120
It's been rough, hasn't it?

160
00:09:26,590 --> 00:09:28,000
Thank you, Subaru.

161
00:09:29,050 --> 00:09:30,040
<i>Who are you?</i>

162
00:09:30,520 --> 00:09:32,080
For saving me.

163
00:09:32,080 --> 00:09:33,270
<i>What?</i>

164
00:09:33,270 --> 00:09:35,160
<i>What? What? What's going on?</i>

165
00:09:35,160 --> 00:09:35,860
Subaru...

166
00:09:35,860 --> 00:09:38,580
<i>Who are you? Who are you? Who are you?</i>

167
00:09:38,580 --> 00:09:41,900
May the blessing of the spirits be with you.

168
00:09:38,580 --> 00:09:41,900
<i>Who are you? Who are you? Who are you?</i>

169
00:09:45,640 --> 00:09:48,480
I think you're much more amazing than me.

170
00:09:51,420 --> 00:09:54,560
Why do you always save me?

171
00:10:08,660 --> 00:10:11,250
Sorry. I'm fine now.

172
00:10:11,250 --> 00:10:14,600
Really? Well, as long as you feel better.

173
00:10:14,600 --> 00:10:16,720
But don't worry me so much, you hear?

174
00:10:16,720 --> 00:10:19,030
Sure. Sorry.

175
00:10:20,680 --> 00:10:23,950
And... about what you asked me...

176
00:10:26,790 --> 00:10:28,880
There is a girl I like.

177
00:10:29,500 --> 00:10:33,180
So... I'll be okay now.

178
00:10:40,690 --> 00:10:42,680
I remember everything now.

179
00:10:42,680 --> 00:10:46,950
What I was so freaked out about, 
and why I was cowering in fear.

180
00:10:47,940 --> 00:10:51,420
No, that's not right. I already knew all of it.

181
00:10:51,880 --> 00:10:54,460
I knew, but I was pretending 
I didn't see it.

182
00:10:55,710 --> 00:11:01,170
I wanted you and Mom to call out my weakness,
 since I was the only one in pain.

183
00:11:02,420 --> 00:11:05,020
To tell me I'm an unbelievably 
small person,

184
00:11:05,020 --> 00:11:06,700
an idiot who's never good enough,

185
00:11:06,700 --> 00:11:08,890
and a self-righteous scumbag.

186
00:11:08,890 --> 00:11:12,850
I wanted you both to beat that 
into me and make me give up.

187
00:11:13,700 --> 00:11:18,170
I've always had this way of somehow managing 
to squeak through anything, you know?

188
00:11:19,090 --> 00:11:21,070
Like in schoolwork and sports.

189
00:11:25,600 --> 00:11:28,330
<i>You're definitely his kid!</i>

190
00:11:28,840 --> 00:11:31,080
But... I don't know when it started...

191
00:11:31,800 --> 00:11:35,210
But I was no longer the best at 
things I used to be the best at.

192
00:11:36,690 --> 00:11:39,710
What used to be my "best" 
grew smaller and smaller.

193
00:11:42,090 --> 00:11:45,520
I started thinking that it all made no sense.

194
00:11:46,400 --> 00:11:49,060
Working my hardest at school seemed stupid.

195
00:11:49,060 --> 00:11:51,660
And why is being a fast runner 
something to brag about?

196
00:11:52,480 --> 00:11:56,760
Making everyone laugh seemed way cooler to me,

197
00:11:56,760 --> 00:11:57,900
and I was way better at it.

198
00:11:58,240 --> 00:12:00,900
<i>You're definitely his kid!</i>

199
00:12:01,180 --> 00:12:03,910
But if I kept that up, it became apparent

200
00:12:04,430 --> 00:12:07,080
that I'd always have to do 
something bigger the next time.

201
00:12:07,800 --> 00:12:09,620
I didn't want people to think I was boring.

202
00:12:10,700 --> 00:12:12,720
I thought I could do anything.

203
00:12:13,330 --> 00:12:15,560
I made everyone think I <i>would</i> do anything.

204
00:12:16,010 --> 00:12:19,740
And so the things I did got dumber and dumber.

205
00:12:20,460 --> 00:12:22,920
I was just out of control, 
not thinking about anything.

206
00:12:27,140 --> 00:12:29,600
I knew they were a bunch of idiots.

207
00:12:30,030 --> 00:12:31,500
I wanted them to think

208
00:12:31,500 --> 00:12:34,310
that they couldn't have this much 
fun if they weren't with me.

209
00:12:34,310 --> 00:12:36,470
That they could regret whatever they wanted,

210
00:12:36,470 --> 00:12:39,640
as long as we spent the boring times 
doing pointless crap for fun.

211
00:12:39,640 --> 00:12:42,240
I decided I would set my sights higher.

212
00:12:46,010 --> 00:12:49,950
But the next thing I knew, 
I was looking around...

213
00:12:50,930 --> 00:12:52,900
And there was no one left but me.

214
00:12:55,790 --> 00:12:58,890
That's when I finally realized

215
00:13:00,260 --> 00:13:05,730
that there was nothing special about me at all.

216
00:13:16,150 --> 00:13:18,750
You're definitely his kid!

217
00:13:25,720 --> 00:13:30,210
From then on, I just spent all 
my time trying not to stand out.

218
00:13:31,500 --> 00:13:33,960
That's how I got through middle school,

219
00:13:34,620 --> 00:13:35,950
then when I got into high school...

220
00:13:38,200 --> 00:13:41,980
I gotta say, I really blew 
my high school debut.

221
00:13:41,980 --> 00:13:43,470
But it was bound to happen.

222
00:13:43,960 --> 00:13:47,340
I'd never had any real 
relationships up to that point.

223
00:13:47,340 --> 00:13:49,470
High school wasn't gonna be any better.

224
00:13:51,280 --> 00:13:53,850
And then it occurred to me...

225
00:13:55,620 --> 00:13:59,540
I just... didn't want to go to school.

226
00:14:02,700 --> 00:14:05,040
It all just snowballed from there.

227
00:14:05,720 --> 00:14:08,850
One day a week of skipping school 
turned into one in every three days,

228
00:14:08,850 --> 00:14:10,810
then every other day...

229
00:14:11,520 --> 00:14:16,120
It didn't take even three months 
before I stopped going at all.

230
00:14:17,360 --> 00:14:22,570
But no matter how pathetic I was, 
you and Mom still treated me

231
00:14:23,140 --> 00:14:24,500
the same as always.

232
00:14:25,320 --> 00:14:27,700
That's what scared me most of all.

233
00:14:28,260 --> 00:14:31,270
I wanted you to say, "I don't love you."

234
00:14:31,270 --> 00:14:32,960
"I despise you."

235
00:14:33,490 --> 00:14:36,890
"You're not my son."

236
00:14:37,870 --> 00:14:40,980
I wanted you to tell me that and throw me out.

237
00:14:41,640 --> 00:14:44,730
I wanted you to make me give up.

238
00:14:47,740 --> 00:14:48,720
But...

239
00:14:48,720 --> 00:14:50,690
<i>It is easy to give up.</i>

240
00:14:51,690 --> 00:14:55,000
<i>But it doesn't suit you.</i>

241
00:14:58,300 --> 00:15:01,940
I love you, Subaru-kun.

242
00:15:03,200 --> 00:15:04,860
Let's start here,

243
00:15:05,690 --> 00:15:06,680
from square one.

244
00:15:07,250 --> 00:15:08,120
No...

245
00:15:08,920 --> 00:15:09,930
From zero!

246
00:15:10,870 --> 00:15:11,780
Right!

247
00:15:11,780 --> 00:15:15,510
My hero is the greatest in the world!

248
00:15:19,310 --> 00:15:20,410
Subaru...

249
00:15:25,270 --> 00:15:27,380
Father Headbutt!

250
00:15:28,810 --> 00:15:32,160
See that, Subaru? That was my 
most loving Father Headbutt,

251
00:15:32,160 --> 00:15:33,830
packed with all my rage!

252
00:15:32,160 --> 00:15:35,080
That was an axe kick! 
Nothing about that was a headbutt!

253
00:15:35,080 --> 00:15:37,590
My leg goes up pretty high, huh?

254
00:15:38,240 --> 00:15:41,400
But you know, you're pretty dumb, aren't ya?

255
00:15:41,400 --> 00:15:42,500
H-Huh?

256
00:15:42,800 --> 00:15:46,100
A lot about what you said bothers me,
 but you know what's the worst?

257
00:15:46,100 --> 00:15:47,460
You wanted me to hate you,

258
00:15:47,460 --> 00:15:50,260
so you tried to achieve that by 
playing hooky? Are you dumb?!

259
00:15:50,260 --> 00:15:53,310
And if you want to get me to throw 
you out, pick a more active method!

260
00:15:53,310 --> 00:15:57,100
Who would ditch their own kid just 
because he retreated into his shell?!

261
00:15:57,100 --> 00:15:59,880
You're so twisted, you're on the 
fast track to being an idiot!

262
00:15:59,880 --> 00:16:03,230
I'd be glad to set you straight 
by force if you want...

263
00:16:04,070 --> 00:16:06,340
But it looks like you've already
 been knocked down

264
00:16:06,340 --> 00:16:09,630
and stood yourself back up, so there's no need.

265
00:16:13,740 --> 00:16:17,060
Remember what I said? I found a girl I like.

266
00:16:17,570 --> 00:16:22,500
Plus, there's a girl who said she 
loved me, despite the way I am.

267
00:16:23,910 --> 00:16:28,550
And neither one of them knows 
I'm the son of Natsuki Kenichi.

268
00:16:29,200 --> 00:16:32,940
In their eyes, I'm just Natsuki Subaru.

269
00:16:33,590 --> 00:16:36,390
No, in all of their eyes...

270
00:16:37,210 --> 00:16:38,780
I was Natsuki Subaru.

271
00:16:40,260 --> 00:16:42,230
I finally figured that out.

272
00:16:42,980 --> 00:16:45,040
Well, it took you long enough.

273
00:16:45,040 --> 00:16:47,940
You're just now coming around 
to saying all this?

274
00:16:47,940 --> 00:16:48,710
I should whack you.

275
00:16:48,710 --> 00:16:51,720
You just whacked my skull 
with your heel a second ago!

276
00:16:51,720 --> 00:16:53,170
Sorry about that.

277
00:16:53,170 --> 00:16:59,040
Still, this was my fault for not realizing 
that you thought so highly of your awesome dad.

278
00:16:59,040 --> 00:17:02,450
Sorry I was just too big a part of your life!

279
00:17:02,450 --> 00:17:05,210
I <i>really</i> don't want to admit 
that's true, even though it is!

280
00:17:05,800 --> 00:17:08,960
But that took a little of the 
weight off my shoulders.

281
00:17:09,370 --> 00:17:12,880
Now all that's left to talk about is 
the future. We've only just begun.

282
00:17:12,880 --> 00:17:16,920
Oh, sure. Um, sorry for putting you through—

283
00:17:15,770 --> 00:17:18,160
If you feel sorry, all you gotta do

284
00:17:18,160 --> 00:17:21,310
is take your time making it up to us.

285
00:17:22,960 --> 00:17:26,890
Take good care of your mom 
and me when we're old,

286
00:17:28,080 --> 00:17:29,230
my eldest son.

287
00:17:40,750 --> 00:17:42,410
I-I'm sorry.

288
00:17:43,190 --> 00:17:44,170
Subaru?

289
00:17:44,580 --> 00:17:45,880
I'm sorry.

290
00:17:45,880 --> 00:17:47,620
I... I...

291
00:17:49,180 --> 00:17:50,920
I... can't...

292
00:17:50,920 --> 00:17:53,420
I-I'm sorry.

293
00:17:54,240 --> 00:17:59,590
I won't be able to make anything up to 
you before... I never see you again.

294
00:18:00,120 --> 00:18:01,550
I'm sorry.

295
00:18:01,550 --> 00:18:03,700
I-I'm sorry, I'm sorry...

296
00:18:04,220 --> 00:18:07,450
I'm so sorry... I'm so sorry.

297
00:18:08,320 --> 00:18:09,910
I'm so sorry!

298
00:18:09,910 --> 00:18:13,730
No matter how much time passes, 
you're still such a handful, son.

299
00:18:13,730 --> 00:18:15,100
Sheesh.

300
00:18:23,230 --> 00:18:26,410
I still feel like walking a little more,

301
00:18:26,410 --> 00:18:28,520
so I'm going to take the long way home.

302
00:18:29,320 --> 00:18:31,910
Okay. I'll head home myself, then.

303
00:18:37,520 --> 00:18:38,840
Hey, Subaru...

304
00:18:39,320 --> 00:18:42,360
I'm sure you have a lot going on, too,

305
00:18:42,360 --> 00:18:45,430
so there's only one thing I want to say.

306
00:18:46,210 --> 00:18:47,490
Give it your all!

307
00:18:48,220 --> 00:18:50,270
I'm expecting the best from you, son.

308
00:18:51,160 --> 00:18:54,190
Yeah. You can count on me, Dad.

309
00:18:56,020 --> 00:18:58,750
My name is Natsuki Subaru,

310
00:18:58,750 --> 00:19:00,870
son of Natsuki Kenichi!

311
00:19:01,470 --> 00:19:04,870
So I can do anything, 
and I <i>will</i> do anything!

312
00:19:05,360 --> 00:19:07,660
'Cause your son's just that awesome!

313
00:19:08,800 --> 00:19:12,860
I know that. You're half me, after all.

314
00:19:24,560 --> 00:19:27,370
The student Natsuki Subaru is complete.

315
00:19:27,960 --> 00:19:30,640
What's it been, about three months?

316
00:19:39,490 --> 00:19:41,450
Oh? Are you nervous?

317
00:19:42,130 --> 00:19:44,950
Want to eat some mayonnaise with me?

318
00:19:43,950 --> 00:19:44,950
Su

319
00:19:45,240 --> 00:19:47,630
I'm not in the mood right now.

320
00:19:47,630 --> 00:19:49,250
I guess not.

321
00:19:49,250 --> 00:19:53,420
You don't actually like mayonnaise 
that much, after all.

322
00:19:53,920 --> 00:19:54,380
Huh?

323
00:19:54,860 --> 00:19:59,840
Your dad and I both like it, so you
 were just sharing it with us.

324
00:19:59,840 --> 00:20:01,930
Wh-What gives you that—

325
00:20:01,930 --> 00:20:05,070
Then which would you choose: 
the world or mayonnaise?

326
00:20:05,070 --> 00:20:06,520
The world, obviously!

327
00:20:06,520 --> 00:20:07,350
You see?

328
00:20:07,350 --> 00:20:09,220
Why do you look so self-satisfied?!

329
00:20:09,470 --> 00:20:12,720
Anyone who picks mayonnaise doesn't 
do it because they like mayonnaise!

330
00:20:12,720 --> 00:20:14,560
They just hate the world!

331
00:20:15,610 --> 00:20:16,940
That's true.

332
00:20:17,910 --> 00:20:20,620
Well, I'm gonna head out.

333
00:20:20,620 --> 00:20:22,560
You're leaving for school now?

334
00:20:22,560 --> 00:20:26,600
I'm glad, but... won't that 
draw some negative attention?

335
00:20:26,600 --> 00:20:28,760
Why not put off until tomorrow 
what can wait until tomorrow?

336
00:20:28,760 --> 00:20:32,080
Your son finally found the motivation 
to do something! Don't ruin this!

337
00:20:32,080 --> 00:20:35,470
I'm already too hard on everyone 
else and easy on me as it is!

338
00:20:35,470 --> 00:20:38,170
Well, if you really were like that,

339
00:20:38,700 --> 00:20:43,130
it would've meant a lot less trouble for me.

340
00:20:48,850 --> 00:20:51,710
And why are you following me?!

341
00:20:51,710 --> 00:20:54,090
Walking to school with my 
mom when I'm trying to

342
00:20:54,090 --> 00:20:56,070
get over being a shut-in is 
worse than a game penalty!

343
00:20:56,070 --> 00:20:58,200
I'm not going all the way to school.

344
00:20:58,200 --> 00:21:00,110
Just to the convenience store.

345
00:21:01,350 --> 00:21:05,610
It's been a long time since you 
and I walked together, hasn't it?

346
00:21:05,610 --> 00:21:06,780
Has it?

347
00:21:07,410 --> 00:21:09,720
What did you and your dad talk about?

348
00:21:09,720 --> 00:21:11,780
Nothing special.

349
00:21:11,780 --> 00:21:13,370
Just reliving the past and stuff.

350
00:21:13,750 --> 00:21:15,090
Hmm...

351
00:21:15,090 --> 00:21:18,920
And reliving the past made 
you want to go to school?

352
00:21:18,920 --> 00:21:21,190
Well, I guess you could say that.

353
00:21:21,190 --> 00:21:24,260
It gave me a chance to look 
back on some things, so...

354
00:21:24,640 --> 00:21:29,850
So you've given up on trying to be just 
like your father in everything?

355
00:21:31,080 --> 00:21:33,390
You were always a hard worker,

356
00:21:33,390 --> 00:21:35,600
and you could do a lot of 
things with minimal effort.

357
00:21:36,160 --> 00:21:38,960
Since your dad was so blindly 
into lots of different things,

358
00:21:38,960 --> 00:21:41,050
you had quite a few opportunities.

359
00:21:41,520 --> 00:21:43,170
Exhausting, isn't it?

360
00:21:43,950 --> 00:21:46,460
Mom, just how much do you...

361
00:21:49,220 --> 00:21:51,200
You know, Subaru,

362
00:21:51,200 --> 00:21:56,210
parents watch their kids much 
more closely than they realize.

363
00:21:56,700 --> 00:21:59,900
I'm always watching you, too, Subaru.

364
00:22:00,650 --> 00:22:04,000
I gave you a suppository 
once when you were little,

365
00:22:04,000 --> 00:22:06,480
so I've even seen your butthole.

366
00:22:06,480 --> 00:22:09,460
Um, sorry, but this was a 
nice conversation up until now.

367
00:22:09,460 --> 00:22:10,760
You don't have to say <i>everything</i> you think.

368
00:22:11,110 --> 00:22:15,320
The mayonnaise, too, and your 
reasons for not going to school...

369
00:22:15,860 --> 00:22:19,740
If there was anything I could have 
done for you, I gladly would have,

370
00:22:20,120 --> 00:22:24,400
but it seemed like nothing 
I tried would have worked out.

371
00:22:25,410 --> 00:22:26,150
But...

372
00:22:26,570 --> 00:22:31,890
Someone who isn't me or your father 
did something for you, didn't they?

373
00:22:32,430 --> 00:22:35,760
I think that's a wonderful thing.

374
00:22:35,760 --> 00:22:37,820
We should be grateful to them.

375
00:22:39,930 --> 00:22:42,370
Yeah, that's right.

376
00:22:42,370 --> 00:22:44,670
That's why I'm able to walk this path right now.

377
00:22:44,670 --> 00:22:46,550
They're really good people.

378
00:22:47,020 --> 00:22:48,470
I don't deserve them.

379
00:22:48,930 --> 00:22:51,600
But you won't give them to anyone else, right?

380
00:22:51,600 --> 00:22:53,360
You better believe it!

381
00:22:53,360 --> 00:22:56,510
It's not about whether I'm 
good enough for them or not.

382
00:22:56,510 --> 00:23:00,480
If I had to give them away, I'd make them mine,
 even if I don't deserve them!

383
00:23:00,480 --> 00:23:03,210
I'd just make myself worthy of them after.

384
00:23:03,860 --> 00:23:05,230
Uh-huh...

385
00:23:06,520 --> 00:23:09,900
You're definitely his kid.

386
00:23:14,960 --> 00:23:17,980
Am I... doing all right?

387
00:23:19,110 --> 00:23:22,620
Am I living up to the expectations for his kid?

388
00:23:24,940 --> 00:23:26,820
You don't have to worry.

389
00:23:26,820 --> 00:23:30,860
Half of you is me, after all.

390
00:23:31,260 --> 00:23:35,970
So if you become even half as cool as 
your dad, you've filled your quota.

391
00:23:36,550 --> 00:23:39,540
Get half as cool as your dad,

392
00:23:40,040 --> 00:23:43,480
and the other half can just be Subaru.

393
00:23:45,980 --> 00:23:50,460
That means you can just do 
your best in your own way.

394
00:23:50,460 --> 00:23:52,180
At least, that's what I think.

395
00:23:54,200 --> 00:23:57,450
In my own way... huh?

396
00:23:57,740 --> 00:23:58,920
That's right.

397
00:23:58,920 --> 00:24:01,880
You can want to be like your mom and dad

398
00:24:01,880 --> 00:24:03,650
as you become Subaru.

399
00:24:05,910 --> 00:24:09,960
Well, I'm heading this way. 
Will you be okay on your own?

400
00:24:09,960 --> 00:24:11,680
I'll be fine.

401
00:24:11,680 --> 00:24:12,670
I see.

402
00:24:13,220 --> 00:24:15,170
Well, give it your all, then.

403
00:24:24,640 --> 00:24:25,760
Mom!

404
00:24:27,930 --> 00:24:29,980
There's something I need to do!

405
00:24:30,400 --> 00:24:33,070
So... I won't see you for a long time!

406
00:24:33,810 --> 00:24:37,340
It's kinda far away... so I don't 
think I'll be able to keep in touch!

407
00:24:37,840 --> 00:24:40,100
But no matter where I am...

408
00:24:40,100 --> 00:24:43,080
I'll be thinking of you guys!

409
00:24:44,040 --> 00:24:46,830
And I'll never... forget you.

410
00:24:47,460 --> 00:24:48,380
Subaru...

411
00:24:48,380 --> 00:24:53,040
I'll never not want to be your kid anymore...

412
00:24:53,040 --> 00:24:56,670
And I don't want to do anything 
that would make me hate myself!

413
00:24:59,810 --> 00:25:01,060
Subaru...

414
00:25:01,680 --> 00:25:03,200
It's okay.

415
00:25:04,690 --> 00:25:08,980
I know what you're trying to say.

416
00:25:09,630 --> 00:25:11,660
You... do?

417
00:25:12,720 --> 00:25:13,570
How?

418
00:25:13,910 --> 00:25:19,350
Well, because I'm your mother, of course.

419
00:25:29,640 --> 00:25:31,810
I'm sorry, Mom.

420
00:25:32,840 --> 00:25:37,800
I was... never able to do anything 
for you guys, and now...

421
00:25:37,800 --> 00:25:41,570
We didn't have you because we wanted 
you to do something for us.

422
00:25:42,680 --> 00:25:45,520
We had you because we wanted 
to do something for <i>you</i>.

423
00:25:46,680 --> 00:25:49,170
I'm... I'm acting like a little kid...

424
00:25:50,080 --> 00:25:51,170
Pathetic...

425
00:25:51,840 --> 00:25:53,860
There's nothing wrong with crying.

426
00:25:54,360 --> 00:25:55,740
You can cry all you want.

427
00:25:56,200 --> 00:26:00,010
As long as you can smile when 
you're done, everything will be fine.

428
00:26:00,650 --> 00:26:04,040
What matters isn't how you start 
or what happens in the middle.

429
00:26:04,690 --> 00:26:06,370
It's how it ends.

430
00:26:09,300 --> 00:26:13,210
You mean as long as things turn out 
okay in the end, nothing else matters?

431
00:26:13,510 --> 00:26:16,740
That's not how I meant for you to take it.

432
00:26:17,160 --> 00:26:19,980
It's a homework assignment from me.

433
00:26:25,450 --> 00:26:27,690
Well... I'm going, then.

434
00:26:37,880 --> 00:26:39,780
Oh, that's right!

435
00:26:39,780 --> 00:26:42,140
Subaru, Subaru! I almost forgot!

436
00:26:45,350 --> 00:26:46,660
Take care.

437
00:26:57,020 --> 00:26:58,090
Take care.

438
00:27:19,520 --> 00:27:20,810
I will!

439
00:27:34,400 --> 00:27:35,290
Okay.

440
00:27:42,640 --> 00:27:46,000
You arrived much earlier than I expected.

441
00:27:46,000 --> 00:27:47,160
Welcome.

442
00:27:48,240 --> 00:27:51,000
So you've had some time to confront your past.

443
00:27:51,000 --> 00:27:53,980
What did it do for you?

444
00:27:54,980 --> 00:27:59,990
Parent and Child

445
00:28:03,980 --> 00:28:13,980


